kde-ai-usage-monitor
====================

This project is a derivative work — an AI-assisted port to Linux and KDE Plasma
of:

    Claude Code Usage Monitor
    https://github.com/CodeZeno/Claude-Code-Usage-Monitor
    Copyright (c) 2025 Craig Constable / Code Zeno Pty Ltd
    Licensed under the MIT License

The upstream project is a Win32 desktop widget written in Rust. This port keeps
its provider-polling layer and replaces everything platform-specific.

Files derived from upstream
---------------------------

  src/providers.rs           <- src/providers.rs (Win32 menu ids removed)
  src/models.rs              <- src/models.rs (reset instants are Unix seconds)
  src/poller.rs              <- src/poller.rs (per-provider results; new
                                ISO 8601 parser covering UTC offsets)
  src/poller/claude.rs       <- src/poller/claude.rs (endpoints and header
                                handling kept; Linux credential discovery)
  src/poller/codex.rs        <- src/poller/codex.rs
  src/poller/cursor.rs       <- src/poller/cursor.rs
  src/poller/opencode.rs     <- src/poller/opencode.rs
  src/poller/antigravity.rs  <- src/poller/antigravity.rs
  src/poller/secret_store.rs <- the Windows Credential Manager reads in
                                src/poller/antigravity.rs, reimplemented over
                                libsecret and KWallet
  src/linux_sqlite.rs        <- src/winsqlite.rs (dlopen instead of raw-dylib)
  src/diagnose.rs            <- src/diagnose.rs
  src/format.rs              <- the duration formatting in src/poller.rs

Written for this project
------------------------

  src/main.rs, src/config.rs, src/cache.rs, src/snapshot.rs,
  plasmoid/**, packaging/**, .github/**

Not ported
----------

Upstream's Win32 window, theme engine, theme studio, tray icon, updater, and
localisation layer have no counterpart here: Plasma draws the widget, themes it,
and updates it through the distribution's package manager.
